{
  "_doc": "EXP-1184: how a LIVE run renders, ONE rule x4 (web lib/coding-session-display.ts, desktop queries::coding_session_display, iOS CodingSessionDisplay.swift, Android CodingSessionDisplay.kt). First match wins: needsInput -> needs_input (amber dot, the run waits on you); agentBusy -> working (the agent's working mark: Claude's frame-stepped spark, or the pulsed brand mark); PR open (status in_review and prState is neither merged nor closed) -> review (green, in review); else -> done (blue: finished with no open PR, or merged). The session row's status never changes for this: a follow-up turn on an in_review run reads working and drops back to review when the turn ends. A paused (offline) run and an ended row are decided by the caller, before this rule. working = status != ended AND state == working (an ended row never animates). statusTone = the list row's status-line tone.",
  "cases": [
